{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"led-matrix-max7219","name":"LED matrix 8x8 (MAX7219)","version":"1.0.1","author":"Bench Workshop","description":"The common red 8x8 LED matrix module with a MAX7219 driver: 64 LEDs from 3 pins (DIN, CS, CLK). Includes LedControl.h for sketches.","category":"Displays","code":"// MAX7219 LED driver with an 8x8 matrix. It listens to every edge on DIN/CLK/CS: data is clocked\n// in on CLK rising edges (16 bits, MSB first) and taken when CS (LOAD) rises: the top byte's low\n// nibble is the register, the low byte its value. Registers: 1-8 = rows, 0x09 decode mode,\n// 0x0A intensity, 0x0B scan limit, 0x0C shutdown (1 = on), 0x0F display test.\nbench.device('max7219', (part) => {\n  const leds = part.screen('leds');\n  const rows = new Array(8).fill(0);\n  let shutdown = true, test = false, intensity = 7, scanLimit = 7;\n  let word = 0, bits = 0;\n  const level = { DIN: 0, CLK: 0, CS: 1 };\n  let powered = false, latches = 0;\n\n  const reset = () => {\n    rows.fill(0);\n    shutdown = true; // a MAX7219 starts up switched off\n    test = false;\n    intensity = 7;\n    scanLimit = 7;\n    word = bits = 0;\n  };\n  const latch = () => {\n    latches++;\n    const reg = (word >> 8) & 0x0f, val = word & 0xff;\n    if (reg >= 1 && reg <= 8) rows[reg - 1] = val;\n    else if (reg === 0x0a) intensity = val & 0x0f;\n    else if (reg === 0x0b) scanLimit = val & 0x07;\n    else if (reg === 0x0c) shutdown = !(val & 1);\n    else if (reg === 0x0f) test = !!(val & 1);\n  };\n  const draw = () => {\n    const k = 0.6 + (0.4 * intensity) / 15;\n    const on = `rgb(${Math.round(255 * k)}, ${Math.round(58 * k)}, ${Math.round(42 * k)})`;\n    for (let r = 0; r < 8; r++)\n      for (let c = 0; c < 8; c++) {\n        const lit = powered && (test || (!shutdown && r <= scanLimit && (rows[r] >> (7 - c)) & 1));\n        leds.set(c, r, lit ? on : 0);\n      }\n  };\n\n  return {\n    edges(events) {\n      if (!powered) return;\n      for (const [pin, v] of events) {\n        if (pin === 'CS') {\n          if (!v && level.CS) { word = 0; bits = 0; } // LOAD falls: a new word\n          if (v && !level.CS && bits >= 16) latch(); // LOAD rises: take the last 16 bits\n        } else if (pin === 'CLK' && v && !level.CLK && !level.CS) {\n          word = ((word << 1) | level.DIN) & 0xffff;\n          bits++;\n        }\n        if (pin in level) level[pin] = v;\n      }\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      const vcc = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\n      const now = vcc >= 4;\n      if (now !== powered) {\n        powered = now;\n        if (!now) reset();\n      }\n      for (const p of ['DIN', 'CLK', 'CS']) {\n        const l = io.level(p);\n        if (l !== null && l !== level[p] && !(p === 'CS')) level[p] = l; // (edges keep these current; this catches slow changes)\n      }\n      const cs = io.level('CS');\n      if (cs !== null) level.CS = cs;\n      draw();\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power (VCC needs 4-5.5 V)'];\n      if (test) return ['display test: all on'];\n      if (shutdown) return ['shut down (the program must send shutdown(0, false))'];\n      return [`on, brightness ${intensity}/15, ${latches} writes`];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"LedControl.h":{"classes":["LedControl"],"code":"// LedControl for sketches: the same functions as the Arduino library (Eberhard Fahle's LedControl),\n// talking to MAX7219s over three pins the same way (shiftOut, MSB first, LOAD/CS framing).\n// Runs inside the program's thread: it sees pinMode, digitalWrite, shiftOut... like a sketch does.\nconst OP_NOOP = 0, OP_DECODEMODE = 9, OP_INTENSITY = 10, OP_SCANLIMIT = 11, OP_SHUTDOWN = 12, OP_DISPLAYTEST = 15;\nconst CHAR_TABLE = {\n  '0': 0x7e, '1': 0x30, '2': 0x6d, '3': 0x79, '4': 0x33, '5': 0x5b, '6': 0x5f, '7': 0x70, '8': 0x7f, '9': 0x7b,\n  a: 0x77, b: 0x1f, c: 0x0d, d: 0x3d, e: 0x4f, f: 0x47, h: 0x37, l: 0x0e, p: 0x67, '-': 0x01, '_': 0x08, ' ': 0x00,\n};\n\nclass LedControl {\n  constructor(dataPin, clkPin, csPin, numDevices = 1) {\n    this.mosi = dataPin;\n    this.clk = clkPin;\n    this.cs = csPin;\n    this.max = Math.max(1, Math.min(8, numDevices));\n    this.status = new Array(64).fill(0);\n    pinMode(this.mosi, OUTPUT);\n    pinMode(this.clk, OUTPUT);\n    pinMode(this.cs, OUTPUT);\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, HIGH);\n    for (let i = 0; i < this.max; i++) {\n      this.spiTransfer(i, OP_DISPLAYTEST, 0);\n      this.setScanLimit(i, 7);\n      this.spiTransfer(i, OP_DECODEMODE, 0);\n      this.clearDisplay(i);\n      this.shutdown(i, true); // starts switched off, like the real chip\n    }\n  }\n  getDeviceCount() { return this.max; }\n  shutdown(addr, b) { if (this.ok(addr)) this.spiTransfer(addr, OP_SHUTDOWN, b ? 0 : 1); }\n  setScanLimit(addr, limit) { if (this.ok(addr) && limit >= 0 && limit < 8) this.spiTransfer(addr, OP_SCANLIMIT, limit); }\n  setIntensity(addr, intensity) { if (this.ok(addr) && intensity >= 0 && intensity < 16) this.spiTransfer(addr, OP_INTENSITY, intensity); }\n  clearDisplay(addr) {\n    if (!this.ok(addr)) return;\n    for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) {\n      this.status[addr * 8 + i] = 0;\n      this.spiTransfer(addr, i + 1, 0);\n    }\n  }\n  setLed(addr, row, column, state) {\n    if (!this.ok(addr) || row < 0 || row > 7 || column < 0 || column > 7) return;\n    const val = 0x80 >> column;\n    const i = addr * 8 + row;\n    this.status[i] = state ? this.status[i] | val : this.status[i] & ~val;\n    this.spiTransfer(addr, row + 1, this.status[i]);\n  }\n  setRow(addr, row, value) {\n    if (!this.ok(addr) || row < 0 || row > 7) return;\n    this.status[addr * 8 + row] = value & 0xff;\n    this.spiTransfer(addr, row + 1, value & 0xff);\n  }\n  setColumn(addr, col, value) {\n    if (!this.ok(addr) || col < 0 || col > 7) return;\n    for (let row = 0; row < 8; row++) this.setLed(addr, row, col, (value >> (7 - row)) & 1);\n  }\n  setDigit(addr, digit, value, dp) {\n    if (!this.ok(addr) || digit < 0 || digit > 7 || value > 15) return;\n    let v = CHAR_TABLE[value.toString(16)] ?? 0;\n    if (dp) v |= 0x80;\n    this.status[addr * 8 + digit] = v;\n    this.spiTransfer(addr, digit + 1, v);\n  }\n  setChar(addr, digit, value, dp) {\n    if (!this.ok(addr) || digit < 0 || digit > 7) return;\n    let v = CHAR_TABLE[String(typeof value === 'number' ? String.fromCharCode(value) : value).toLowerCase()] ?? 0;\n    if (dp) v |= 0x80;\n    this.status[addr * 8 + digit] = v;\n    this.spiTransfer(addr, digit + 1, v);\n  }\n  ok(addr) { return addr >= 0 && addr < this.max; }\n  spiTransfer(addr, opcode, data) {\n    // one 16-bit word per chip in the chain; the chip at `addr` gets this one, the others a no-op\n    const words = new Array(this.max * 2).fill(0);\n    words[addr * 2 + 1] = opcode;\n    words[addr * 2] = data;\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, LOW);\n    for (let i = this.max * 2; i > 0; i--) shiftOut(this.mosi, this.clk, MSBFIRST, words[i - 1]);\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, HIGH);\n  }\n}\nvoid OP_NOOP;\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"matrix8x8","name":"LED matrix 8x8 (MAX7219)","description":"64 red LEDs driven by a MAX7219. Wire VCC to 5 V, GND, and DIN / CS / CLK to any three pins; in a sketch: #include <LedControl.h>, LedControl lc(DIN, CLK, CS, 1); lc.shutdown(0, false); lc.setLed(0, row, col, true);","swatch":"#d0302a","mass":12,"shape":[{"box":[3.25,0.16,5],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1f5fbf"},{"box":[3.2,0.75,3.2],"at":[0,0.535,-0.6],"color":"#1b1b1d"},{"screen":{"id":"leds","size":[3.1,3.1],"px":[8,8],"on":"#ff3a2a","off":"#2a0e0c","bg":"#151517"},"at":[0,0.912,-0.6]},{"box":[0.7,0.1,0.7],"at":[0,0.21,1.55],"color":"#151618","collide":false}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VCC","GND","DIN","CS","CLK"],"at":[-0.508,0.16,2.3],"kinds":{"VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","DIN":"in","CS":"in","CLK":"in"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (4-5.5 V)","vmin":4,"vmax":5.5}}}],"device":"max7219"}]}